<article class="env-lemma" id="0BTJ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0BTJ">Lemma <span data-tag="0BTJ">41.20.1</span>.</a> If $f : X \to S$ is surjective, then the functor (<a href="/tag/0BTI" data-tag="0BTI">41.20.0.1</a>) is faithful. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $a, b : U_1 \to U_2$ be two morphisms between schemes étale over $S$. Assume the base changes of $a$ and $b$ to $X$ agree. We have to show that $a = b$. By Proposition <a href="/tag/024V" data-tag="024V">41.6.3</a> it suffices to show that $a$ and $b$ agree on points and residue fields. This is clear because for every $u \in U_1$ we can find a point $v \in X \times _ S U_1$ mapping to $u$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>